{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast","id":1294095,"title":"In Bloodlines, the main character got really strong, really fast.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-05T10:04:07-08:00","id":1294095,"title":"In Bloodlines, the main character got really strong, really fast.","content":"He was fighting a Bodhisattva, a Tzimiche an etc.<br /> <br /> How would a vampire that was so new get so strong that fast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T15:57:14-08:00","id":1294199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magicballz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast#post1294095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was fighting a Bodhisattva, a Tzimiche an etc.<br /> <br /> How would a vampire that was so new get so strong that fast?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He DID NOT fight Bohsaattva she was at best a Mandarin.<br /> <br /> But clearly his ST ran each day as a separate Game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T18:14:28-08:00","id":1294264,"title":"","content":"Mostly its just a video game using video game pacing and ignoring the TT game.<br /> <br /> However, there are hints in the game that there is some sort of external force involved. LaCroix goes from easily using Dominate on the player, to it not working as if the player was a lower Generation than the Prince suddenly.<br /> <br /> There are popular fan theories about the true identity of the cab driver, and if he's as powerful as some of them would imply, he'd have access the ability to aid in the player's power and might have purposefully done so slowly to catch the local Kindred off guard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T19:41:23-08:00","id":1294289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast?p=1294264#post1294264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly its just a video game using video game pacing and ignoring the TT game.<br /> <br /> However, there are hints in the game that there is some sort of external force involved. LaCroix goes from easily using Dominate on the player, to it not working as if the player was a lower Generation than the Prince suddenly.<br /> <br /> There are popular fan theories about the true identity of the cab driver, and if he's as powerful as some of them would imply, he'd have access the ability to aid in the player's power and might have purposefully done so slowly to catch the local Kindred off guard.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He's been having you commit diablerie during those black out periods and wiping your memories","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T22:24:34-08:00","id":1294327,"title":"","content":"Or just feeding you his Blood, the blood of 3rd gens is known (in fluff) to improve thickness of generation of someone","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T11:59:15-08:00","id":1294465,"title":"","content":"I thought he just had the game set on easy mode. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T12:28:13-08:00","id":1294476,"title":"","content":"The taxi driver was Cain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 03-23-2019, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T23:20:06-08:00","id":1295224,"title":"","content":"It probably helped that the PC was some kind of mutant, given that their Disciplines were built fully and completely around making them a combat monster. Even letting them do things with basic Disciplines that those Disciplines are NOT supposed to do, going by the tabletop. Like summoning spectral beasts to aid them. Or forcing folks to commit suicide. Not to mention a weird Path of Thaumaturgy (that the character apparently didn't need to study?) that does the Path of Blood, except entirely combat related (what I like to call &quot;The Path of Martial Blood&quot;).<br /> <br /> There's a LOT going on with the protagonist of Bloodlines, not just their meteoric rise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T00:46:32-08:00","id":1295522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast?p=1295224#post1295224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It probably helped that the PC was some kind of mutant, given that their Disciplines were built fully and completely around making them a combat monster. Even letting them do things with basic Disciplines that those Disciplines are NOT supposed to do, going by the tabletop. Like summoning spectral beasts to aid them. Or forcing folks to commit suicide. Not to mention a weird Path of Thaumaturgy (that the character apparently didn't need to study?) that does the Path of Blood, except entirely combat related (what I like to call &quot;The Path of Martial Blood&quot;).<br /> <br /> There's a LOT going on with the protagonist of Bloodlines, not just their meteoric rise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I Kind of want to make an Auspex variant based on it that does make you better at shooting because psychic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T13:14:39-07:00","id":1295619,"title":"","content":"Again, there's plenty of video-game design realities one has to deal with when considering things like Disciplines don't stuff they don't do in the TT versions.<br /> <br /> Even if the game wasn't so combat heavy and you could solidly beat the game in other fashions... there's plenty of Discipline powers in the books that are basically not worth implementing in a video game and need to be replaced with something else.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Though simple house rule for shoot Auspex? Allow Auspex 1 to increase your dice gained for each aiming action by your Auspex rating, and if would go over your cap, you can aim at fast moving targets.<br /> <br /> Basically makes it the sniper Discipline, which is fun without getting too nasty.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T20:47:45-07:00","id":1295729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast?p=1295619#post1295619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, there's plenty of video-game design realities one has to deal with when considering things like Disciplines don't stuff they don't do in the TT versions.<br /> <br /> Even if the game wasn't so combat heavy and you could solidly beat the game in other fashions... there's plenty of Discipline powers in the books that are basically not worth implementing in a video game and need to be replaced with something else.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Though simple house rule for shoot Auspex? Allow Auspex 1 to increase your dice gained for each aiming action by your Auspex rating, and if would go over your cap, you can aim at fast moving targets.<br /> <br /> Basically makes it the sniper Discipline, which is fun without getting too nasty.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Maybe something like allowing &quot;auto&quot; aiming like you always gain the buffs of aiming without having to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-10T22:58:50-07:00","id":1295743,"title":"","content":"Allowing aiming in a split action (it's already automatic and all) always feels like it should be an Auspex + Celerity combo. Especially since by itself it's only +1 die, +3 if you're using a scoped weapon, unless you have an aiming booster like my above suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T05:31:12-07:00","id":1295768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast?p=1295743#post1295743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allowing aiming in a split action (it's already automatic and all) always feels like it should be an Auspex + Celerity combo. Especially since by itself it's only +1 die, +3 if you're using a scoped weapon, unless you have an aiming booster like my above suggestion.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was thinking something like you have a &quot;natural&quot; scope with your senses so you functionally are always capable of taking aim(and taking aim won't make it better)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-11T09:54:52-07:00","id":1295858,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what that's supposed to do/mean.<br /> <br /> You're always already allowed to aim with ranged weapons without a scope. Scopes only let you get to your aim cap faster. My initial suggestion is, effectively, giving Auspex 1 an additional power of having a 'natural' scope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T04:38:09-07:00","id":1296372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast?p=1294264#post1294264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, there are hints in the game that there is some sort of external force involved. LaCroix goes from easily using Dominate on the player, to it not working as if the player was a lower Generation than the Prince suddenly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe they were the same Generation and he just fails the check because the character's Willpower increased, thus changing the difficulty. Maybe even gaining the Iron Will merit along the way due to their extreme circumstances. Also keep in mind the nature of the commands necessitating greater number of successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T09:31:17-07:00","id":1296435,"title":"","content":"Except, of course, none of that exists in the game to indicate that happened.<br /> <br /> What we know, is that he (a) activates Dominate based on the animations and (b) is completely caught off guard that it doesn't work when it did before.<br /> <br /> He doesn't act like someone that just failed his roll (and the question of if the animation should reflect that), or didn't roll enough successes. He's completely and utterly gobsmacked that his Dominate doesn't work on you at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T15:34:11-07:00","id":1296531,"title":"","content":"How does a Character know a roll failed, only the player does","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T21:27:41-07:00","id":1296593,"title":"","content":"If I shoot a gun and it misses what I was aiming at... I know I missed, which is failing in the system.<br /> <br /> LaCroix's dialogue is pretty specific: he believes that his ability to Dominate you doesn't work anymore. He's aware because he tries and it doesn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T22:37:30-07:00","id":1296609,"title":"","content":"Ok, I'll run with your example.<br /> You fire a gun; it doesn't hit the target.<br /> <br /> Do you know if you were aiming poorly, (Got Zero Successes)<br /> The target moved better than you could aim (They got more successes than you did)<br /> the bullet was a blank (external influence)<br /> or Angels (or Caine) moved the bullet around the target so you never had a chance in the first place?<br /> <br /> In general - you just know the result the bullet didn't hit, the dominate didn't work.<br /> Could have been a bad role, could never have worked even with a dozen successes; The Player may know but the Character doesn't<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T00:25:49-07:00","id":1296618,"title":"","content":"The position you're advocating is nonsensical.<br /> <br /> An experience shooter is going to be able to observe the difference between a shot that was a wide miss, and a shot that was good but the target ducked undercover in the last second. They're going to know the feel difference of a blank suddenly being in their gun after they fire it. They're going to be able to see a bullet impact behind their target without hitting their target because of magical intervention.<br /> <br /> Do they know the strict mechanical results? Of course not. Do they know the observable nature of what happened and how? Yeah, they do.<br /> <br /> LaCroix is an experienced Dominate user. He knows the difference between not having the power of the blood behind his words, and his target not being subject to his powers.<br /> <br /> And most importantly? He says it. He knows. He clearly reacts to something he can observe: that he can't Dominate you any more. You can argue that's not something that the TT rules allow someone to figure out (though I say let someone roll if you're not going to let them feel it, there are traits that would cover this), but it's how Bloodlines works, because that's what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T00:43:41-07:00","id":1296621,"title":"","content":"Nothing in any of the games imply that the user has any indication on why a failure on mind control happened. There's no text anywhere to back up your position. It's a fine house rule but not something that even the lore will back you up on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T02:33:37-07:00","id":1296633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PazuzuAxelf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast?p=1296621#post1296621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing in any of the games imply that the user has any indication on why a failure on mind control happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, there's plenty, as the games generally portray vampires as aware of things like Dominate not working on those of lower Generation, and working better on the weak-willed/broken than strong minded individuals, and eye-contact being necessary.<br /> <br /> Know 100% like the players do? No. Have the ability to make educated guesses that are largely accurate? Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's no text anywhere to back up your position. </div> </div> </div>Please cite any text that goes against it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a fine house rule but not something that even the lore will back you up on. </div> </div> </div><b>IT HAPPENS IN THE GAME WE'RE TALKING ABOUT</b>.<br /> <br /> What more lore do I need?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T02:57:13-07:00","id":1296637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast?p=1296633#post1296633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please cite any text that goes against it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Burden of proof falls upon the one making the claim - you. I cannot easily disprove a negative. I might as well just say &quot;read the whole book&quot;. If you are saying there are game rules to support your position then <u>you</u> need to provide the text and page numbers in which it appears. My position is that they are not there at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast?p=1296633#post1296633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>IT HAPPENS IN THE GAME WE'RE TALKING ABOUT</b>.<br /> <br /> What more lore do I need?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, this was a bit rude. I'll respond but please temper your responses with civility.<br /> <br /> I believe your interpretation is incorrect. I'll quote myself here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or maybe they were the same Generation and he just fails the check because the character's Willpower increased, thus changing the difficulty. Maybe even gaining the Iron Will merit along the way due to their extreme circumstances. Also keep in mind the nature of the commands necessitating greater number of successes. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12710,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","user":"PazuzuAxelf","date":". 03-14-2019, 06:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T03:02:13-07:00","id":1296639,"title":"","content":"I'd add that the protagonist can actually outright state that LaCroix's dominate won't work on them anymore. I agree with Heavy Arms, everything in the scene indicates that it's something more serious than simply failing to use a power. I mean, he also tries a few times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T04:14:11-07:00","id":1296643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PazuzuAxelf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast?p=1296637#post1296637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Burden of proof falls upon the one making the claim - you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how the burden of proof works.<br /> <br /> One side doesn't carry all the burden of proof just for 'going first' in making a claim.<br /> <br /> You claimed: &quot;Nothing in any of the games imply that the user has any indication on why a failure on mind control happened. There's no text anywhere to back up your position.&quot;<br /> <br /> The burden of proof falls on you to back this up, not me. I made my case (which you seem to forget is that the game hints that the player character's massive power is due to external influence; LaCroix and Dominate is evidence to support my claim, not my claim itself).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I cannot easily disprove a negative. </div> </div> </div>Doesn't really matter does it? If you want to go one about burdens of proof, there are plenty of basic guides out there of how to rhetorically handle a negative claim to an acceptable standard in an informal discussion. Falling back on the difficulty of burden of proof on a negative when you chose to make a negative claim isn't my fault. It's yours to address to make your counterargument cogent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you are saying there are game rules to support your position then <u>you</u> need to provide the text and page numbers in which it appears. </div> </div> </div>I didn't make the claim you're saying I need to back up.<br /> <br /> To be more clear for you: I'm asserting that the game defaults to not dictate what the character knows or doesn't know about the results and leaves it to the flow of the narrative and character preconceptions. <br /> <br /> An experienced Dominate user is going to have failed, and botched, and accidentally tried to Dominate someone of a lower Generation over the centuries. They're going to have the ability to call on that experience to intuit why a failure happened. In the TT rules, this is backed up by having traits like Awareness and Occult to judge your character's mystic intuitions and supernatural knowledge.<br /> <br /> The game also rarely suggests making rolls in secret for the player (ex: Presence 3), because they are situations where the character would not have a way to gauge their success/failure. Dominate isn't one of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, this was a bit rude. I'll respond but please temper your responses with civility. </div> </div> </div>Maybe consider that I felt I was responding with the level of civility I was getting? Civility isn't just word choice or fonts. &quot;You're wrong because I said so, and I don't have to prove why.&quot; is really fucking rude in my book.... and basically your whole argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe your interpretation is incorrect. </div> </div> </div>That's nice. You haven't actually cited what's wrong with it. You've just cited examples of traits that Bloodlines doesn't use, and the abstract possibility of a failed roll without the context of the scene itself (where LaCroix clearly believes he used the power).<br /> <br /> Also.... the command in that scene is actually simpler (he's demanding you give him the key) than some of the earlier ones (where he forces you to go do errands for him if you try to refuse).... so that context further undercuts the idea that it was a hard roll that he failed without realizing it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T16:45:33-07:00","id":1297605,"title":"","content":"I will concede that the firearms example isn't a perfect example. However, that's because we don't have a &quot;real Life&quot; example for how mind control does or does not work.<br /> The Evidence we have is that La Croix has successfully Dominated &quot;The PC&quot; before.<br /> - La Croix tried, but couldn't dominate the PC this time.<br /> ***La Croix _Believes_ he now can't dominate the PC.***<br /> <br /> Could be external changes, could be PC Changes (Stats combining for target number now higher, spending a willpower if allowed, a power gained, generation improved etc), could be a botch giving the impression that the PC can't be Dominated ever again.<br /> If we accept <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>' claim that, as an experienced Dominate user, La Croix would know what a failure looks like (Based on Failure on dice) then I don't see any other applicable facts or options<br /> <br /> I still say that &quot;The PC's Generation&quot; becoming better is not the Only possible cause of Dominate not-working and La Croix thinking he can't ever dominate him. But I don't think there's enough to say what exactly the cause is<br /> <br /> <br /> **** I personally don't believe that characters will always know what a failure is compared to not enough successes or external influence, just that it didn't seem to work, or wasn't good enough. You can be as convincing as possible for instance and not know why someone didn't come around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T18:59:07-07:00","id":1297624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast?p=1297605#post1297605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still say that &quot;The PC's Generation&quot; becoming better is not the Only possible cause of Dominate not-working and La Croix thinking he can't ever dominate him. But I don't think there's enough to say what exactly the cause is</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's not really the point.<br /> <br /> The point is the PC suddenly becoming either immune or highly resistant to Dominate out of the blue, which indicates some sort of external influence on events as the PC hasn't done anything that would cause that on their own (even if the external influence is to empower the PC, such as a NPC that has the ability to use the equivalent of Path of Blood 3 on another character instead of themself).<br /> <br /> How it happened beyond not being something the PC did on their own (which there is no evidence of in the game) is what matters, not the specific mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T21:06:10-07:00","id":1297635,"title":"","content":"His response could still have been due to a botch, character having put lots of XP into the skills/Willpower that form the difficulty. It's not purely external as options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T22:20:02-07:00","id":1297644,"title":"","content":"I agree with PazuzuAxelf and Illithid on this one. If the text doesn't outright say &quot;you know if your attempt works automatically&quot;, one must assume that the characters are operating from a state of ignorance by default. That's how Real Life works: humans are, by default, ignorant of everything.<br /> <br /> And no, being aware that Dominate fails on lower gen targets is not the same as automatically being aware of any failure of the Discipline. Because the explanation that requires fewer assumptions is that Vampires &quot;know&quot; that Dominate fails against those with lower gen because of experience. They've had thousands of years of trial and error to understand how their powers work. They know that lower gens are immune to Dominate because while the Discipline may sometimes fail on equal or higher gens, it ALWAYS fails on the lower. That's not a special knowledge that the Discipline must impart on the person, that's just observation.<br /> <br /> My stance is &quot;when it doubt, assume ignorance&quot;. A vampire using Dominate can stare into someone's eyes and order them around all night. They only know if it succeeds or fails based on the target's subsequent behavior. Hell, Dominate 3 (at least in V20) states that memory reading and alteration are not the result of some kind of telepathic contact, but rather the vampire asking questions and the subject responding, as if under hypnosis. There's no reason to believe any other Dominate power would work otherwise.<br /> <br /> LaCroix was surprised that his Dominate failed because the PC wasn't immediately doing his bidding. A person is allowed to be surprised at failure, especially they are confident in their abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T23:40:46-07:00","id":1297649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast?p=1297635#post1297635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">His response could still have been due to a botch, character having put lots of XP into the skills/Willpower that form the difficulty. It's not purely external as options.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;botching Dominate makes your target immune from your Dominate&quot; was dropped as a Discipline-wide rule in the game before Bloodlines came out. So, unless we're going to assume 1e and 2e rules randomly apply when convenient, a botch doesn't explain the totality of the scene; it would take the rather unlikely occurrence of multiple botches.<br /> <br /> You spend XP on your character when you play the game, no XP is spent on Willpower. Even so, by the rules, there's no way to raise WP that fast even with unlimited XP because you can't raise the same trait multiple times without significant narrative breaks.<br /> <br /> And before you respond remember to answer this:<br /> <br /> Why does it matter?<br /> <br /> All of this is over the assertion that Bloodines <b>HINTS</b> that there are external forces helping the player character, and things like the sudden Dominate fails by LaCroix are one of the scenes that <b>HINTS</b> at this. I wouldn't be stressing &quot;hints&quot; so fucking much if the game just said, &quot;yeah Jack and the Cabbie totally used blood powers to help you,&quot; directly, because then it wouldn't be, &quot;the game hints,&quot; but, &quot;the game says.&quot;<br /> <br /> You are arguing all of this over &quot;hints&quot; as if &quot;hints&quot; doesn't acknowledge that it's possible the hinting in a red herring or Easter egg by calling it a hint in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast?p=1297644#post1297644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with PazuzuAxelf and Illithid on this one. If the text doesn't outright say &quot;you know if your attempt works automatically&quot;, one must assume that the characters are operating from a state of ignorance by default. That's how Real Life works: humans are, by default, ignorant of everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>No that isn't how life works. You're claiming that humans, by default, botch every roll they make.<br /> <br /> Since every instances is ultimately unique, and we are ignorant, we never know how to respond no matter what our previous experience, and thus mush screw up everything we do. That's what &quot;are default ignorant&quot; means if you start applying it to things like simple actions as the ST system defines them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And no, being aware that Dominate fails on lower gen targets is not the same as automatically being aware of any failure of the Discipline. </div> </div> </div>Arguing strawmen doesn't help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not a special knowledge that the Discipline must impart on the person, that's just observation. </div> </div> </div>Or, in other words, you're arguing against yourself because this is not a position of ignorance even if it isn't a position of absolute knowledge either.<br /> <br /> If you always assume ignorance, nobody would figure anything out by observation because ignorance would stop them from connecting dots. They'd be ignorant of the deductive process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They only know if it succeeds or fails based on the target's subsequent behavior. </div> </div> </div>But we're not talking about whether or not LaCroix knows it failed, because he does because it's obvious when it doesn't work. The debate is whether, after lots of observation using the power, LaCroix could make a decent guess as to why it failed. Bloodlines is written in a fashion that indicates he can. Hell that the player character can and the player character is new to all of this and might not even have Dominate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's no reason to believe any other Dominate power would work otherwise. </div> </div> </div>Yes, there is, because the book describes how the other powers operate and they don't have the conversational nature of Dominate 3. Dominate 1 and 2 are as long as it takes to state the order to the target. Dominate 4 only requires regular social interactions with the target not hypnotizing them. Dominate 5 likewise doesn't involve conversation, just staring into the subject's eyes until they run out of Willpower and you can take them over. Basically the other powers are more 'binary' in that they work, or they don't, where Dominate 3 is fuzzier. Of course Dominate 3 also says that vampires can sense that it's already been used on a target...not really a 'default of ignorance' there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T18:54:58-07:00","id":1298455,"title":"","content":"I like to think the protagonist got so strong because he or she diablerized the entirety of the Sabbath in LA.<br /> <br /> Consider this: Every time you went into a combat zone and had to fight vampires, you probably killed a fair share of those vampires by feeding on them, draining them dry. Every time you did that, you committed diablerie. That's how your character got so strong. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T21:28:02-07:00","id":1298490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1294095-in-bloodlines-the-main-character-got-really-strong-really-fast?p=1298455#post1298455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to think the protagonist got so strong because he or she diablerized the entirety of the Sabbath in LA.<br /> <br /> Consider this: Every time you went into a combat zone and had to fight vampires, you probably killed a fair share of those vampires by feeding on them, draining them dry. Every time you did that, you committed diablerie. That's how you